          <div class="cycle-steps">
            <div>
              <div class="cycle-step-head">
                <span class="cycle-step-num step-teal">1</span>
                <h3 class="cycle-step-title">Capture</h3>
              </div>
              <div class="prose-ki">
                <p>Information arrives without immediate judgment. The Port receives everything — email, notes, links, conversations — before the Library decides what belongs. The principle here is separation: receiving is not the same as deciding.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="cycle-step-head">
                <span class="cycle-step-num step-accent">2</span>
                <h3 class="cycle-step-title">Connect</h3>
              </div>
              <div class="prose-ki">
                <p>Material is contextualised and linked to existing knowledge. This is the transformation step — where received information becomes owned knowledge. Links form. Meaning emerges. A Stream becomes a Pillar note.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="cycle-step-head">
                <span class="cycle-step-num step-ok">3</span>
                <h3 class="cycle-step-title">Reflect</h3>
              </div>
              <div class="prose-ki">
                <p>Periodic review surfaces what's stale, updates what's changed, and retires what's obsolete. Reflection is not optional — it is how the island stays honest about what it knows. Without it, islands accumulate archaeology rather than knowledge.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
